--- machine\system\eventd
canonical: Machine\System\eventd

eventd's storage, ingestion and query policy. The six path values are required;
all tuning values have compiled defaults. Invalid live changes are ignored and
the last valid value remains effective. Unknown values are ignored.

The standard deployment is offered by `eventd-config.reg`; installing the
package does not apply it. Store paths and socket paths require a restart.
Every tuning value below applies live.

--- machine\system\eventd eventstorepath
canonical: Machine\System\eventd EventStorePath
type: REG_SZ
default: (required; standard /var/state/eventd/events/)
applies: restart

Provisioned protected directory holding event shards and `eventd-meta.db`.
Must be an absolute path with no symbolic-link component.

--- machine\system\eventd logstorepath
canonical: Machine\System\eventd LogStorePath
type: REG_SZ
default: (required; standard /var/state/eventd/logs/)
applies: restart

Provisioned protected directory holding `logs.db`.

--- machine\system\eventd metricstorepath
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MetricStorePath
type: REG_SZ
default: (required; standard /var/state/eventd/metrics/)
applies: restart

Provisioned protected directory holding `metrics.db`.

--- machine\system\eventd querysocketpath
canonical: Machine\System\eventd QuerySocketPath
type: REG_SZ
default: (required; standard /run/eventd/query.sock)
applies: restart

Unix stream socket serving authorized observability queries.

--- machine\system\eventd logsocketpath
canonical: Machine\System\eventd LogSocketPath
type: REG_SZ
default: (required; standard /run/eventd/log.sock)
applies: restart

Unix datagram socket receiving service log records, including peinit output.

--- machine\system\eventd metricsocketpath
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MetricSocketPath
type: REG_SZ
default: (required; standard /run/eventd/metric.sock)
applies: restart

Unix datagram socket receiving metric samples.

--- machine\system\eventd walcheckpointpages
canonical: Machine\System\eventd WalCheckpointPages
type: REG_DWORD
default: 1000
valid: 100 to 100000
applies: live

WAL pages that trigger a passive checkpoint on event, log, metric and metadata
databases. Lower values bound WAL size more tightly but checkpoint more often.

--- machine\system\eventd storageshards
canonical: Machine\System\eventd StorageShards
type: REG_DWORD
default: 0
valid: 0 to 256
applies: restart

Active event shard count. Zero selects one shard per attached KMES buffer.

--- machine\system\eventd maxbatchsize
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MaxBatchSize
type: REG_DWORD
default: 10000
valid: 100 to 100000
applies: live

Maximum event rows considered for one durability transaction.

--- machine\system\eventd maxbatchlatencyms
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MaxBatchLatencyMs
type: REG_DWORD
default: 100
valid: 10 to 5000
applies: live

Maximum event batch age in milliseconds before commit.

--- machine\system\eventd logmaxbatchsize
canonical: Machine\System\eventd LogMaxBatchSize
type: REG_DWORD
default: 5000
valid: 100 to 100000
applies: live

Maximum log records per transaction.

--- machine\system\eventd logmaxbatchlatencyms
canonical: Machine\System\eventd LogMaxBatchLatencyMs
type: REG_DWORD
default: 500
valid: 10 to 5000
applies: live

Maximum log batch age in milliseconds before commit.

--- machine\system\eventd maxlogdatagrambytes
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MaxLogDatagramBytes
type: REG_DWORD
default: 262144
valid: 262144 to 1048576
applies: live

Largest accepted log datagram. Oversized datagrams are discarded before
decoding. The 262144-byte minimum is the portable PSPU producer contract and
cannot be lowered.

--- machine\system\eventd metricmaxbatchsize
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MetricMaxBatchSize
type: REG_DWORD
default: 5000
valid: 100 to 100000
applies: live

Maximum metric samples per transaction.

--- machine\system\eventd metricmaxbatchlatencyms
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MetricMaxBatchLatencyMs
type: REG_DWORD
default: 1000
valid: 10 to 5000
applies: live

Maximum metric batch age in milliseconds before commit.

--- machine\system\eventd maxmetricdatagrambytes
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MaxMetricDatagramBytes
type: REG_DWORD
default: 262144
valid: 262144 to 1048576
applies: live

Largest accepted metric datagram. The 262144-byte minimum is the portable PSPU
producer contract and cannot be lowered.

--- machine\system\eventd metricseriescachesize
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MetricSeriesCacheSize
type: REG_DWORD
default: 50000
valid: 1000 to 1000000
applies: live

Maximum resolved metric series retained in the in-memory LRU cache.

--- machine\system\eventd metricauthorizationcachesize
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MetricAuthorizationCacheSize
type: REG_DWORD
default: 16384
valid: 256 to 1000000
applies: live

Maximum cached metric publication verdicts. Entries are keyed by the KACS
token ID and modified ID plus metric name, and all entries are invalidated
when the eventd Security descriptor generation changes.

--- machine\system\eventd adaptiveindexwindowhours
canonical: Machine\System\eventd AdaptiveIndexWindowHours
type: REG_DWORD
default: 24
valid: 1 to 168
applies: live

Rolling query-accounting window used by adaptive event indexes.

--- machine\system\eventd adaptiveindexpolicyintervalminutes
canonical: Machine\System\eventd AdaptiveIndexPolicyIntervalMinutes
type: REG_DWORD
default: 60
valid: 60 to 1440
applies: live

Interval between adaptive-index policy recomputations. The one-hour floor
prevents index churn.

--- machine\system\eventd adaptiveindexcreatethreshold
canonical: Machine\System\eventd AdaptiveIndexCreateThreshold
type: REG_DWORD
default: 100
valid: 10 to 10000
applies: live

Queries on a field within the accounting window needed to request an index.

--- machine\system\eventd adaptiveindexdropthreshold
canonical: Machine\System\eventd AdaptiveIndexDropThreshold
type: REG_DWORD
default: 10
valid: 1 to 1000 and below AdaptiveIndexCreateThreshold
applies: live

Queries below which a requested index is removed. The gap from the creation
threshold supplies hysteresis.

--- machine\system\eventd sheddingwindowseconds
canonical: Machine\System\eventd SheddingWindowSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 30
valid: 10 to 300
applies: live

Sliding batch-pressure window used for graduated index shedding.

--- machine\system\eventd sheddingbatchpercent
canonical: Machine\System\eventd SheddingBatchPercent
type: REG_DWORD
default: 75
valid: 50 to 100
applies: live

Percentage of batches above three quarters full that triggers shedding.

--- machine\system\eventd emergencysheddingbufferpercent
canonical: Machine\System\eventd EmergencySheddingBufferPercent
type: REG_DWORD
default: 75
valid: 50 to 95
applies: live

KMES ring fill percentage that drops all adaptive indexes during a maximum-size
batch. The mandatory timestamp index is never shed.

--- machine\system\eventd eventretentiondays
canonical: Machine\System\eventd EventRetentionDays
type: REG_DWORD
default: 30
valid: 1 to 3650
applies: live

Maximum event age in days.

--- machine\system\eventd eventretentionmaxbytes
canonical: Machine\System\eventd EventRetentionMaxBytes
type: REG_QWORD
default: 0
valid: 0 or more
applies: live

Maximum logical live bytes across event shards. Zero disables the size limit.

--- machine\system\eventd logretentiondays
canonical: Machine\System\eventd LogRetentionDays
type: REG_DWORD
default: 14
valid: 1 to 3650
applies: live

Maximum log age in days.

--- machine\system\eventd logretentionmaxbytes
canonical: Machine\System\eventd LogRetentionMaxBytes
type: REG_QWORD
default: 0
valid: 0 or more
applies: live

Maximum logical live bytes in the log store. Zero disables the size limit.

--- machine\system\eventd metricretentiondays
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MetricRetentionDays
type: REG_DWORD
default: 90
valid: 1 to 3650
applies: live

Maximum metric sample age in days.

--- machine\system\eventd metricretentionmaxbytes
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MetricRetentionMaxBytes
type: REG_QWORD
default: 1073741824
valid: 0 or more
applies: live

Maximum logical live bytes in the metric store. The 1 GiB default bounds a
misconfigured or compromised publisher's label-cardinality growth. Zero
explicitly disables the size limit.

--- machine\system\eventd retentioncheckintervalminutes
canonical: Machine\System\eventd RetentionCheckIntervalMinutes
type: REG_DWORD
default: 60
valid: 1 to 1440
applies: live

Normal interval between retention passes. Storage-full handling may request an
immediate pass independently.

--- machine\system\eventd retentiondeletebatchrows
canonical: Machine\System\eventd RetentionDeleteBatchRows
type: REG_DWORD
default: 10000
valid: 100 to 100000
applies: live

Maximum rows removed by one bounded retention transaction.

--- machine\system\eventd querytimeoutms
canonical: Machine\System\eventd QueryTimeoutMs
type: REG_DWORD
default: 30000
valid: 1000 to 300000
applies: live

Maximum milliseconds for parsing through transmission of an initial query
result. Streaming watch phases are not time-limited.

--- machine\system\eventd maxconcurrentqueries
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MaxConcurrentQueries
type: REG_DWORD
default: 128
valid: 1 to 4096
applies: live

Global concurrent query limit. Excess requests are rejected, not queued.

--- machine\system\eventd maxstreamingqueries
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MaxStreamingQueries
type: REG_DWORD
default: 64
valid: 1 to 1024
applies: live

Global streaming-query limit, enforced in addition to MaxConcurrentQueries.

--- machine\system\eventd maxdistinctstreamvalues
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MaxDistinctStreamValues
type: REG_DWORD
default: 100000
valid: 1000 to 10000000
applies: live

Maximum remembered values for one DISTINCT stream before it is terminated.

--- machine\system\eventd maxqueryrequestbytes
canonical: Machine\System\eventd MaxQueryRequestBytes
type: REG_DWORD
default: 65536
valid: 1024 to 16777216
applies: live

Hard inbound query frame limit, checked before allocating its payload.

--- machine\system\eventd queryresponsetargetbytes
canonical: Machine\System\eventd QueryResponseTargetBytes
type: REG_DWORD
default: 65536
valid: 1024 to 16777216
applies: live

Soft result batching target. One complete record may exceed it and is never
split or truncated.

--- machine\system\eventd crosstypewindowms
canonical: Machine\System\eventd CrossTypeWindowMs
type: REG_DWORD
default: 15000
valid: 1000 to 300000
applies: live

Centred event/log existence window used by cross-type predicates.

--- machine\system\eventd crosstypemaxlookbackseconds
canonical: Machine\System\eventd CrossTypeMaxLookbackSeconds
type: REG_DWORD
default: 604800
valid: 3600 to 2592000
applies: live

Largest historical range accepted for a cross-type query.

--- machine\system\eventd\security
canonical: Machine\System\eventd\Security

Query access policy. `Events`, `Logs` and `Metrics` contain descriptor values
under identifier patterns; the most specific dot-prefix match wins and `*` is
the fallback. `Admin` governs the EVENTD_ADMINISTER right used by `INDEX`.
eventd provisions defaults only when the corresponding entries do not exist.
Descriptor changes apply to the next query.
